ious":"10:03:51","deltaSeconds":793}}},"historicalRank":{"fieldSizeRank":3,"finishersRank":8,"finishRateRank":93,"winningTimeRank":19,"winningTimeRankDir":14,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1966,"mensWinner":"Tommy MALONE","mensTime":"06:14:07"}},"narrative":"The 2010 Comrades Marathon was the 85th running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.208 km. The race was held on Sunday, 30 May. Conditions: Cloudy early morning, warming to hot and cloudless at midday. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nStephen MUZHINGI claimed the men's title in 05:29:01, ahead of Ludwick MAMABOLO (05:35:29) and Bongmusa MTHEMBU (05:37:49). Elena NURGALIEVA won the women's race in 06:13:04, followed by Olesya NURGALIEVA (06:13:05).\n\nElena NURGALIEVA's 06:13:04 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1966 (Tommy MALONE, 06:14:07).\n\nFrom a field of 23,533 entries, 14,330 runners crossed the finish line (60.9% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 11,203 men and 3,127 women (21.8% female). The average finish time was 10:17:04.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 12 Wally Hayward, 598 Silver, 2,304 Bill Rowan, 6,557 Bronze, 4,839 Vic Clapham. 3,767 runners (26.3%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Frikkie BOTHA in 11:59:59.\n\nThis edition featured the 3rd largest field in race history. Compared to the previous down run in 2009, the field was 81.8% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 55% of the finishers, with 6,387 seniors (avg 10:03:00) and 7,943 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}